C62 patch -- wire the search box into the gallery window (two files, no new
dependencies). Generated with git diff against main@4ae3b38 and verified with
"git apply --check" and a real PrismArchive build.

The card itself delivers the MODEL (Src/PrismCore/SearchBoxModel.hpp) and the
DRAWING INSTRUCTIONS (Src/PrismWin/SearchBoxPainter.hpp) plus their tests. This
patch is the wiring C60 can apply verbatim when it finishes the window rework;
nothing here changes the model's rules.

What it does:
  * Ctrl+F -> Command::OpenSearch (the ONE key table, Shortcuts.hpp) opens the
    field and switches the view to list mode, because the filtered rows are the
    list;
  * WM_CHAR feeds committed text, WM_KEYDOWN maps Backspace/Delete/arrows/
    Home/End/Esc/Enter, and WM_IME_* feeds the composition PREVIEW (GCS_COMPSTR)
    and the commit (GCS_RESULTSTR) -- the window never edits bytes itself;
  * the query owns FilterSpec::substring only, so search narrows an existing
    type/size/glob filter instead of resetting it; an empty query restores the
    rows;
  * the painter's instruction list is built each frame from the layout and the
    same model the keys edit; DrawSearchBox is the only Direct2D knowledge;
  * hit testing is Scene::HitTest on the SAME instructions that were painted.

Known limits, on purpose:
  * the search covers the CURRENT folder's list view (item.path names), not the
    whole catalog; widening it is a row-projection change in the window, not a
    model change -- SearchBoxModel already speaks catalog indices;
  * the field's rectangle is a 320 x 32 DIP box at the content's top-right; C60
    owns the final placement (action band vs content), so SearchBounds is one
    function;
  * the injected measure callback uses the window's crumb format (15 px), so
    the caret/badge rectangles match what DrawText paints; a DPI-aware target
    should pass its real DWrite format and DPI.

Contracts touched: D1 (stdout marker untouched), D3/D26/D27 (the model's own
mutants still decide the C62 suite), B1 ((std::max) parenthesised), B2 (headers
include what they use), D7 (whole-block additions, no index surgery).
Apply:  git apply tools/patches/c62-search-wire.patch

